[38;5;231m⏺[39m Added a basic checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m:

  - A [38;5;153m<label class="task">[39m wrapping a native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m and a [38;5;153m<span class="task-label">[39m. Wrapping in the
    label means clicking the text toggles the box too.
  - One CSS rule ([38;5;153m.task input:checked + .task-label[39m) strikes through and greys the text when checked. On/off state is
    the native checkbox's — no JavaScript.

  To add more items, copy the [38;5;153m<label class="task">[39m block; the styling applies automatically.

  No tests were run — the repo has no test setup or build. I verified the change by inspection only, not in a browser.

